synopsis:
  Expose `data Unit` and `data TupleN` from `Data.Tuple` in `base`
description:
  The data types `data Unit` and `data TupleN` (for N from 2 to 64) are now exported from
  `Data.Tuple` in the `base` library instead of `Data.Tuple.Experimental` in `ghc-experimental`.
  See `CLC proposal 442 <https://github.com/haskell/core-libraries-committee/issues/442>`_.
